<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says gives tax breaks to housing projects.</title>
<headline>Manila says gives tax breaks to housing projects.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Board of Investments (BOI) had decided to give tax and duty incentives to developers of low cost housing in the country, documents released by the agency on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>The BOI will include low cost housing projects in the list of the country's 1997 Investment Priorities Plan (IPP), the documents said.</p>
<p>IPP is an annual list of preferred areas of economic activities given tax and fiscal incentives by the government.</p>
<p>The BOI plans to give four-year income tax holidays and a minimum three percent duty on the importation of capital equipment and machineries for the construction of low-cost housing projects.</p>
<p>Low-cost housing projects include the sale of housing units in the range of 375,000 to 500,000 pesos each, the BOI said.</p>
<p>-Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
